From 826b82cf1e8b3bd9accbe3c439d2d3cdb07dda06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rogerbacardit <rogerbacardit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:26:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Twister: stepped params by position, push = preset value,
 track colours, paced output

- Twister knobs 9-16 drive an enum / switch / int of 2-32 values by the
  ring's position (one zone per value); continuous params keep relative
  steps (midi/ext-param.ts, ext-param-steps.ts).
- Push on encoders 9-16 returns the parameter to its value when the preset
  was loaded; bases forgotten on a preset change (encoder 3 or knob 1 on
  the preset page).
- A ring being turned is not resynced for 350 ms, so the follow no longer
  fights the hand on stepped params.
- All output to the Twister goes through a paced, coalescing queue
  (midi/ext-out.ts, 10 messages per tick, flushed from tick()): a full
  repaint is 43 messages and a burst lost everything past one USB packet.
- The 10 s wake gap counts only the Twister's own CCs (ch 1/2, CC 0-15),
  not a KeyStep's on the same hub.
- Track colours: tracks 1-4 green, blue, orange, purple, rotated across
  groups; the Twister's assigned rings wear the active track's colour
  (midi/ext-colors.ts). This palette is the user's preference for their
  device: it breaks track-colors.mjs's separation rules (blue/purple, and
  green/orange under CVD), so it is not meant for upstream as is.

Gate: local suites green (logic, app-loop, perf, screenshot, source-rules,
fleet-pages, grid-cost, device-scripts, host-globals) except abi-parity,
red before this change too; typecheck clean. Deployed ui.js only and
checked by the user on the device; device tier not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
